+------------------------------------------------------------
-- @DESC: malformed lambda without arrow rejected (E6)
------------------------------------------------------------+
rule main:
  new bad := λ(x);
return;
+------------------------------------------------------------
Negative case: a `λ` header must be `λ(params) => (body)`.
Here the parameter list closes immediately — the parser never
sees the `=>`/body, so it must report E0009 and exit non-zero
(spec/07-functions.md §2.1 lambda_expr grammar).
------------------------------------------------------------+
-- @AI: No - negative syntax case (passes on non-zero exit)
